    <v:String x:Key="PatchNotesPage_MorePatchNotes">More patch notes</v:String>
    <v:String x:Key="PatchNotesPage_MorePatchNotesBeta">More beta patch notes</v:String>
    <v:String x:Key="FaqPage_Title">FAQ</v:String>
    <v:String x:Key="FaqPage_Subtitle">Quick answers about safety, temp files, the Store build, and what the launcher repairs by itself.</v:String>
    <v:String x:Key="FaqPage_Q1_Title">Is it safe?</v:String>
    <v:String x:Key="FaqPage_Q1_Text">Yes. The launcher works around the official Minecraft for Windows app, downloads addons, and lets Windows open them normally. It also checks the official VC++ runtime if your PC is missing it.</v:String>
    <v:String x:Key="FaqPage_Q2_Title">Why does it use TEMP files?</v:String>
    <v:String x:Key="FaqPage_Q2_Text">TEMP is only used as a quick parking spot for addon downloads and the Microsoft VC++ installer. Once the file is needed, Windows opens it and the launcher can clean up the leftovers more easily.</v:String>
    <v:String x:Key="FaqPage_Q3_Title">Why do I need Minecraft for Windows from Microsoft Store?</v:String>
    <v:String x:Key="FaqPage_Q3_Text">Because XylarBedrock targets only the official Microsoft Store release. If the real game is not installed, the launcher does not unlock the main flow.</v:String>
    <v:String x:Key="FaqPage_Q4_Title">What does crash recovery actually repair?</v:String>
    <v:String x:Key="FaqPage_Q4_Text">If the last session ends badly, the next boot clears broken addon downloads, wipes stale launcher temp files, reloads the addon cache, and refreshes the bundled mod pack before normal use.</v:String>

